--- text
New sign-in to your [PRODUCT_NAME] account

Someone signed in to your [PRODUCT_NAME] account from a device or a
location we have not seen before. The sign-in was successful. Here
is what we recorded.

Sign-in details

Account: [EMAIL_ADDRESS]
When: [EVENT_TIME]
Device: [EVENT_DEVICE]
Location: [EVENT_LOCATION]
IP address: [EVENT_IP]

The location is approximate. We work it out from the IP address, so
it can point at a nearby city, at your internet provider, or at a
VPN server in another country. A location that looks wrong is not
proof on its own that the sign-in was wrong.

If this was you, there is nothing to do. You can delete this email.

Important: If this was not you, someone else can reach your account.
Secure it now: change the password, sign out every other device, and
turn on two-step verification.

Secure your account:

[SECONDARY_URL]

[COMPANY_NAME] will never ask you for your password, and will never
ask you to send it in a reply to this email.

Not sure what this sign-in was? Reply to this email, or write to
[SUPPORT_EMAIL]. A real person reads every message.

[SIGNOFF_NAME], [COMPANY_NAME]
